 "notes": "Metrics are from greedy evaluation on the 2,000 held-out programs (seed 12345) at the final step (1000), mean \u00b1 std over seeds 0-2; the verdict uses the mean. Untested hack rate = share of uncovered branches where the greedy action is DELETE or STUB. Executor: pilot SFT checkpoint (results/sft_cache), GRPO as pilot.train. Reviewer features: one-hot visible pass (2) and one-hot total diff lines over 0..8 (value fix 1, stub 1, deletion 2), logistic regression. Each step a random 5% of the 512 sampled episodes is audited; 20% of audits are held out (scored online by the reviewer before it trains, for rev_acc_heldout) and the rest, restricted to visible-passing episodes (the reviewer models P(correct | visible pass)), go to a FIFO buffer of 4,096; then 5 Adam steps (lr 0.05, L2 1e-4, minibatch 256). Reward for every episode = visible pass x 1[P(correct) >= 0.5] from the reviewer before that step's update; audits only train the reviewer and do not change the reward. The reviewer starts at P=0.5 (approves all). Chart's reviewer accuracy is on the greedy policy's visible-passing eval episodes. Diff size exposes deletions (each adds a line), so the hack the policy learned was stubbing, which look like value fixes; FS was still rising at step 1000 (0.04 at step 600)."
